### 3. Copy the prompt

Attach the inventory file you just downloaded to your assistant, then copy the prompt below. It tells the assistant to use the inventory as the source for facility-specific claims and to keep unrecorded details explicit.

<div style="position: relative; margin-bottom: 20px;">
  <button id="copy-prompt-btn" class="md-button md-button--primary" style="position: absolute; top: 10px; right: 10px; z-index: 10;">Copy prompt</button>
  <textarea id="generated-prompt" rows="18" style="width: 100%; padding: 15px; padding-top: 50px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--md-default-fg-color--light); background-color: var(--md-code-bg-color); font-family: monospace; line-height: 1.5; resize: vertical;" readonly></textarea>
</div>

<script id="plan-experiments-config" type="application/json">
{{ plan_experiments_config_json | safe }}
</script>

<script>
  document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
    const configNode = document.getElementById("plan-experiments-config");
    let pageConfig = {
      facility_short_name: "Core Imaging Facility",
      facility_contact_url: "#",
      facility_contact_label: "Contact Core Imaging Facility Staff",
      llm_inventory_asset_url: "assets/llm_inventory.json",
    };
    try {
      if (configNode?.textContent?.trim()) {
        pageConfig = JSON.parse(configNode.textContent);
      }
    } catch (error) {
      console.error("Failed to parse plan-experiments config", error);
    }

    const facilityShortName = String(pageConfig?.facility_short_name || "Core Imaging Facility");
    const inputArea = document.getElementById("experiment-desc");
    const outputArea = document.getElementById("generated-prompt");
    const copyBtn = document.getElementById("copy-prompt-btn");

    const basePromptTop = `You are helping me explore microscopy options using the attached ${facilityShortName} inventory.

Use the JSON as the only source for facility-specific facts.

Rules:
- Read planning_contract first. It states which route lists are complete and what is not recorded.
- A component missing from a complete route hardware list is not on that route; other missing or null values are unknown.
- Treat llm_context.authoritative_route_contract as route truth. llm_context.route_planning_summary and hardware_focus_summary are convenience views; raw hardware must not override the route contract.
- Never combine components from different routes.
- Objectives are instrument-level unless explicit route compatibility is recorded.
- Preserve unresolved/selectable branches, splitters and endpoints; do not silently choose one.
- Use capability_route_reconciliation and route_family_coverage to relate capabilities such as TIRF, STED or SIM to recorded route families. Do not invent route types.
- The inventory records no booking, access or training availability. Operational/QC status is not booking availability.
- Do not invent performance or suitability. If speed, depth, phototoxicity, sample compatibility, long-run suitability or fluorophore compatibility is not established, label it unknown and say what to confirm.
- You may explain general microscopy principles and trade-offs as general guidance, but never turn them into an ${facilityShortName}-specific performance claim.
- Do not force a ranking when the inventory does not justify one.

Use this procedure:
1. Separate known from unknown facts.
2. Exclude an instrument only when an explicit inventory fact establishes a mismatch.
3. Identify supported candidate routes without inventing suitability.
4. Verify route membership, detector/endpoint and relevant components; report only hardware details that affect the decision.
5. Preserve branch/splitter handling and identify unresolved points that could change the choice.

My request:
`;

    const basePromptBottom = `

Return a concise answer with:
1. What the inventory clearly establishes.
2. A short shortlist of supported candidate instruments/routes; if the inventory cannot narrow the options, say so.
3. For each candidate, only route and hardware details that matter to this request, without mixing routes.
4. Useful objectives only as instrument-level facts unless route compatibility is explicit.
5. One or two important unknowns most likely to change the choice and what to confirm with ${facilityShortName} staff.

Do not force a best microscope or backup when the inventory does not justify one. Do not invent facility specifications.`;

    function updatePrompt() {
      const userText = inputArea.value.trim();
      const desc = userText ? userText : "[Describe what you want to image or measure, in your own words.]";
      outputArea.value = basePromptTop + desc + basePromptBottom;
    }

    inputArea.addEventListener("input", updatePrompt);
    updatePrompt();

    copyBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
      outputArea.select();
      outputArea.setSelectionRange(0, 99999);
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(outputArea.value).then(() => {
        const originalText = copyBtn.innerText;
        copyBtn.innerText = "Copied";
        setTimeout(() => { copyBtn.innerText = originalText; }, 2000);
      }).catch(err => {
        console.error('Failed to copy text: ', err);
      });
    });
  });
</script>

